{"id":"portswigger-web-security-academy--server-side-vulnerabilities--os-command-injection--os-command-injection-simple-case","path":"portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/os-command-injection/os-command-injection-simple-case.md","title":"OS command injection, simple case","category":"portswigger-web-security-academy","source":"https://github.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/blob/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/os-command-injection/os-command-injection-simple-case.md","html":"<h1 id=\"os-command-injection-simple-case\">OS command injection, simple case</h1>\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>This lab contains an OS command injection vulnerability in the product stock checker.</p>\n<p>The application executes a shell command containing user-supplied product and store IDs, and returns the raw output from the command in its response.</p>\n<p>To solve the lab, execute the <code>whoami</code> command to determine the name of the current user.</p>\n<h2 id=\"solution\">Solution</h2>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(49)%20(1).png\" alt=\"OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Every product has a dedicate check function to retrieve if a product is availble or not:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(1)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n\n\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(2)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>We can try to concatenate it with a payload like as ; &amp; or |: <code>;whoami</code></p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(4)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>and we obtain the user of system: peter-Gu9oqX solving the lab.</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(5)%20(1)%20(1).png\" alt=\"OS command injection, simple case screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n","toc":[{"id":"description","title":"Description","level":2},{"id":"solution","title":"Solution","level":2}],"excerpt":"OS command injection, simple case Description This lab contains an OS command injection vulnerability in the product stock checker. The application executes a shell command containing user-supplied product and store IDs,","searchText":"Description Solution"}